+# Design — The Future-Facing Gallery
+
+## Frame system
+
+- Canvas: 1920 × 1080.
+- Safe padding: 120px with the lower 120px reserved for lesson chrome.
+- Background: deep navy architectural field with quiet grid lines and a paper exhibition surface.
+- Foreground density: one large idea, two to four supporting labels, and small gallery metadata per beat.
+
+## Color
+
+- Navy deep `#0a1e2f` and navy `#0d2437` anchor the frame.
+- Paper `#ffffff` and cultured `#f6f6f9` carry readable evidence.
+- Blue `#3393d6` signals forward direction and connection.
+- Gold `#eaab2d` marks selections, outcomes, and the final resolve.
+- Ink `#292f35` is used for text on light cards.
+
+## Typography
+
+- Proxima Nova with system fallback.
+- Display: 96–112px, 900 weight.
+- Heading: 60–68px, 900 weight.
+- Body: 40–46px, 400 weight.
+- Labels: 22px, 700 weight, uppercase, tracked.
+
+## Composition details
+
+- A persistent top-left module marker and top-right `MID-CAREER MOMENTUM` label establish continuity.
+- Thin registration marks, frame numbers, and selection ticks make the gallery feel produced and intentional.
+- Cards use 12px corners and restrained shadows; chips use transparent fill and a 2px blue edge.
+- No gradients, photographic assets, or decorative clutter.
+
+## Motion
+
+- Entrances use 0.45–0.6 second transforms and opacity, with 0.14 second stagger.
+- Each beat exits in 0.3 seconds; background furniture remains stable.
+- Lines draw with scaleX, cards rise 32–48px, and choice markers resolve with a small finite scale pulse.
+- The final gold direction line extends once during the closing second.
